const description: { en: string; ja: string } = {"en":"Two holly leaves standing side by side in a ring, each upright on a short stem: a sharp point at the top and, down each side, four lobes, each ending in a spine that points up with a round bay cut over it. The point is the lens between two circles that cross on the leaf's midrib. Each bay is one circle and each lobe's round edge another: the edge runs from its spine, where it crosses its own bay, down to the next bay, and the last rounds in to the foot of the leaf. A white midrib runs the whole length, and five white veins leave it on each side, each with a branch. The stem is the space between two upright lines under a level one, and the circle of the room inside the ring cuts its foot. The right leaf is built first: the half toward the axis, the stem, then the outer half; the left leaf is built where it stands.","ja":"輪の中に、柊の葉を二枚、左右に並べて立てます。葉は短い柄の上にまっすぐ立ち、上の先はとがり、両側に裂片が四つずつあります。裂片の先は上を向いたとげで、その上に丸い切れ込みがあります。葉の先は、葉のまん中の線の上で交わる二つの円の間の形です。切れ込みは円一つ、裂片の丸い縁は別の円一つです。縁は、自分の切れ込みと交わるとげの先から、下の切れ込みまで続き、いちばん下の縁は、葉の下の端まで丸く続きます。白い葉脈は、まん中に上から下まで一本、その両側に五本ずつあり、どれも途中で二つに分かれます。柄は、横の直線の下の、二本の縦の直線の間で、下の端は輪の内側の円で切ります。右の葉から作図します。中心線に近い半分、柄、外側の半分の順です。左の葉は、その場で作図します。"};

export default construction;
export { construction, description };
